# How this deck was made (W3C PROV-O): researched card by card from the sources below,
# each card checked against at least two of them, then in the review rounds below.
<#compilation>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-04T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:used <https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1221156> ,
              <https://www.bundesrat.de/DE/bundesrat/laender/laender-node.html> ,
              <https://www.migration.gv.at/de/leben-und-arbeiten-in-oesterreich/oesterreich-stellt-sich-vor/geografie-und-bevoelkerung/> ,
              <https://www.ris.bka.gv.at/NormDokument.wxe?Abfrage=Bundesnormen&Gesetzesnummer=10000138&Artikel=108> ,
              <https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/corporate/publications-manuals/discover-canada/read-online/canadas-regions.html> ,
              <https://www.australia.com/en/facts-and-planning/about-australia/cities-states-and-territories.html> ,
              <https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tysklands_f%C3%B6rbundsl%C3%A4nder> ,
              <https://www.ne.se/uppslagsverk/> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <#anton-wiklund> ;
    prov:wasInformedBy <#review-0> ,
                       <#review-1> ,
                       <#review-2> ,
                       <#review-3> ,
                       <#review-4> ,
                       <#review-5> ;
    rdfs:comment "Compiled by Anton Wiklund with the help of AI."@en ,
                 "Sammanställd av Anton Wiklund med hjälp av AI."@sv ,
                 "About this record: the comments on this compilation, its review rounds and its sources are condensed from the deck's dossier, the working record kept while the deck was compiled, from which a provenance report was generated. The dossier's per-card evidence and Wikidata checks, its numbered queries and scripts (its Queries section) and its logs of discrepancies are not part of this release; where the text refers to them, to the dossier or the report, or to findings listed below, it means that record. The builder is the script that built the deck from the dossier and ran its Wikidata checks."@en ,
                 "The cards were checked by machine (live Wikidata and the app's SHACL and DCAT-AP validators)."@en ,
                 "1. Selection and capitals from Wikidata (query 1): every P150 (contains the administrative territorial entity) statement without an end time of Germany (Q183), Austria (Q40), Canada (Q16) and Australia (Q408), with the classes (P31) of each division, its P36 (capital) statements without an end time and their rank, and the English, Swedish and multilingual (mul) labels of division and capital. It returned 16 German divisions, all instances of \"federated state of Germany\" (Q1221156); 9 Austrian ones, all instances of \"federal state of Austria\" (Q261543); 13 Canadian ones, 10 instances of \"province of Canada\" (Q11828004) and 3 of \"territory of Canada\" (Q9357527); and 15 Australian ones: 6 instances of \"state of Australia\" (Q5852411), 3 \"mainland territories of Australia\" (Q14192234: the Australian Capital Territory, the Northern Territory and the Jervis Bay Territory) and 7 external territories. Every division in the deck has exactly one P36 statement without an end time, except Berlin (Q64), Hamburg (Q1055) and Vienna (Q1741), which have none: each is a single item that is both a city and a state (P31 includes Q133442, city-state). Query 2 read the further statements used in notes (Bremen's P150 and the P1448 official names of Klagenfurt and Quebec City) and the class and location of Q21882134, to confirm that this P36 value of Vorarlberg is the town of Bregenz."@en ,
                 "2. Names from Wikidata (the script entities.py, query 3): the Wikidata API (wbgetentities) returned the English, Swedish, multilingual and German labels and aliases, the English and Swedish Wikipedia sitelinks and the claims of every division and capital of query 1 and of the class items. The front is the division's English and Swedish label. The back is the capital's English and Swedish label, with two exceptions: Fredericton (Q2138) has no English label, so its multilingual label is used; the English back of Carinthia is \"Klagenfurt\", the city's multilingual alias and the form the Austrian government table, NE and the Swedish label use, rather than the English label \"Klagenfurt am Wörthersee\", its official name (P1448), which the card gives in a note. The front notes give the federation and the kind of division in the compiler's own short wording, based on the class items Q1221156, Q261543, Q11828004, Q9357527, Q5852411 and Q14192234 (sv labels \"förbundsland\", \"Österrikes förbundsländer\", \"provins i Kanada\", \"territorium i Kanada\", \"delstat i Australien\", \"fastlandsterritorium i Australien\"): \"Förbundsland i Tyskland\", \"Förbundsland i Österrike\", \"Provins i Kanada\", \"Territorium i Kanada\", \"Delstat i Australien\", \"Territorium i Australien\"."@en ,
                 "3. Official checks, one per federation, each page downloaded with curl (queries 4 to 7) and its text read after removing the HTML tags: Germany — the Bundesrat's page \"Die Länder\", whose box for each Land gives \"Hauptstadt: …\" for all 16 (\"Berlin Hauptstadt: Berlin\", \"Freie Hansestadt Bremen Hauptstadt: Bremen\", \"Freie und Hansestadt Hamburg Hauptstadt: Hamburg\"); Austria — the federal government's Migration.gv.at page \"Geografie und Bevölkerung\", whose table (\"Quelle: Statistik Austria (Stand 1.1.2026, vorläufige Daten)\") gives the Landeshauptstadt of eight Länder and a dash for Wien; for Vienna the federal constitution (B-VG Art. 108, from the Austrian legal information system RIS, query 8) was read; Canada — the citizenship guide Discover Canada (Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada), chapter \"Canada's Regions\", whose table lists, per region, the provinces and territories and their capital cities in the same order; Australia — Tourism Australia's page \"Australian States, Territories and Capital Cities\", which names the capital in its section on each state and territory. The Australian government sources tried first gave no list of state capitals: Geoscience Australia's page on the areas of the states and territories and the Australian Bureau of Statistics' page on Greater Capital City Statistical Areas (both fetched, query 7) describe the capital cities without naming each state's capital, so they were not used. Each card's evidence quotes the line or sentence of the official page; the script make_dossier.py asserted that every quote occurs in the saved page text (with tags removed, white space collapsed and a space before a comma or full stop removed)."@en ,
                 "4. Swedish names (queries 9 and 10): the four Swedish Wikipedia list articles \"Tysklands förbundsländer\", \"Österrikes förbundsländer\", \"Kanadas provinser och territorier\" and \"Australiens delstater och territorier\" were fetched as wikitext with their revision ids through the MediaWiki API (svwiki.py) and the division and capital cells of their tables parsed (parse_svwiki.py). For every card the Swedish front equals the name shown in the row and the Swedish back equals the capital's link text (for the city-states, the German table spans the row of Berlin and Hamburg over both columns, with the note \"Berlin och Hamburg är både städer och förbundsländer\", and the Austrian table has a dash for Wien). Nationalencyklopedin was then consulted (fetch_ne.py): the article on each division whose address could be found from its Swedish or English name (34 of the 46; Berlin, Hamburg, Bremen, Brandenburg, Saarland, Schleswig-Holstein, Salzburg, Alberta, Manitoba, Ontario, Saskatchewan and Victoria were not fetched or not found, and those cards rest on Wikidata, the official page and the Swedish Wikipedia), and the articles on München, Hannover, Düsseldorf, Sankt Pölten, Klagenfurt, Eisenstadt, Bregenz, Quebec (the city) and Canberra. The evidence quotes NE's short description phrase (e.g. \"delstat i södra Tyskland\") and, where present, the phrase naming the capital. Where NE's Swedish form differs from the card (Quebec, Newfoundland and Labrador, compounds written with an en dash) the card follows Wikidata's Swedish label and the Swedish Wikipedia; see quality control."@en ,
                 "5. Assembly: make_dossier.py wrote the cards from the saved files: the Wikidata evidence from q1.csv and entities.json, the Swedish Wikipedia evidence from the parsed rows, and the official and NE evidence from the quotes listed in the script, each asserted to be present in the saved page. It also refuses a card whose division is not in query 1, is not an instance of its class, whose capital is not its P36 value, or whose English or Swedish text is not a label, alias or mul label of the item. The Wikidata checks on every card (division labels, class, capital, capital labels, and the statements behind the notes) are run against live Wikidata by the builder on every build."@en ,
                 "6. The city-state convention: where one item is both the city and the state (Berlin, Hamburg, Vienna), the card's answer is the city itself, with the note \"City-state: the city is itself a state\"; the Bundesrat states the same for Berlin and Hamburg (\"Hauptstadt: Berlin\", \"Hauptstadt: Hamburg\"). Bremen is a city-state of two cities whose capital is the city of Bremen (Wikidata P36, the Bundesrat). For Vienna no source names a separate capital (the Austrian table leaves it blank); the card applies the same convention, and its note states the fact the answer rests on, that the city is itself the state."@en ,
                 "Selection: All constituent states of four federations, as of 4 October 2026: the 16 Länder of Germany, the 9 Länder of Austria, the 10 provinces and 3 territories of Canada, and the 6 states and the 2 self-governing mainland territories of Australia (the Australian Capital Territory and the Northern Territory): 46 cards, one per division, each with its one current capital. Left out: Australia's Jervis Bay Territory (a mainland territory without self-government or a capital of its own; the Swedish Wikipedia and Wikidata list it separately) and its seven external territories (Norfolk Island, Christmas Island, the Cocos (Keeling) Islands and others), which are not among the states and self-governing territories of the federation; the federal capitals as such (Berlin, Vienna, Ottawa, Canberra), except where they are themselves a state's capital or a city-state, as noted on those cards; former capitals; and other federations (the United States has its own deck). Conventions: Berlin, Hamburg and Vienna, each a single city that is itself a state, are answered with the city itself (see the method); Canberra is the capital of the Australian Capital Territory as Wikidata and the Swedish Wikipedia list give it. The cards are studied front to back only: \"Victoria\" is both an Australian state (front) and the capital of British Columbia (back), and the city-states have the same name on both sides, so the reverse direction would not always have one answer."@en ,
                 "Licensing: The only content source is Wikidata, whose structured data is CC0: the selection of the 46 divisions, the link from each to its capital, the English and Swedish names, the class names in the front notes and the facts in the back notes all come from it, so the deck is CC0 1.0 like the rest of the library. The Bundesrat, Migration.gv.at, Discover Canada and Tourism Australia (all with copyright terms that allow at most non-commercial reproduction), Nationalencyklopedin (all rights reserved) and the Swedish Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0) were used for verification only, as was the Austrian federal constitution on RIS (not protected by copyright, § 7 UrhG): they confirmed facts that Wikidata gave, and no wording, table or selection was copied from them. The selection is the complete set of constituent states of each federation, shared by any list of them because it is the complete set, not a choice taken from a list. The notes are the compiler's own wording. Quotations in the provenance report's evidence are not part of the deck: they are short verbatim quotations naming their sources (for NE under the Swedish quotation right, Upphovsrättslagen 22 §, and in line with NE's own conditions for quoting)."@en .

<#review-0>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-04T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Sources, licences and machine checks: every card's division, capital and names against Wikidata, the official page of its federation (Bundesrat, Migration.gv.at, Discover Canada, Tourism Australia), the Swedish Wikipedia list and, where found, Nationalencyklopedin; the city-state convention; the Swedish names."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: All 46 cards, the sources and the deck metadata."@en ,
                 "Outcome: Wikidata, the official pages and the Swedish Wikipedia agree on the capital of every division that has one; NE agrees wherever an article was found. No Wikidata check was skipped. The differences found are the city-states (no separate capital in Wikidata, the Austrian table and the Swedish Wikipedia; the Bundesrat names Berlin and Hamburg as their own capitals), a few name forms (Klagenfurt, Quebec City, Yukon, Swedish forms in NE) and the name Victoria on both sides of the deck."@en .

<#review-1>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-04T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Factual accuracy"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: All 46 cards against live Wikidata, the Bundesrat page, German and English Wikipedia lists; the description and notes."@en ,
                 "Outcome: No factual errors. Two wording suggestions: the description listed Berlin, Hamburg and Vienna as \"the city-states\" although Bremen is one too, and the Québec notes said different things in English and Swedish. Both applied."@en .

<#review-2>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-04T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Language, translation and language tags"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: All 46 cards, title, description, keywords and the language tags of the built TTL."@en ,
                 "Outcome: Swedish forms, lower-casing and tags correct. One warning (the description's list of city-states omits Bremen) and three style suggestions (Bremen note, Québec notes, full stops); all applied."@en .

<#review-3>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-04T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Licensing, attribution and documentation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: Sources, licence evidence, the method, queries and selection, the evidence quotes against re-fetched pages, the built TTL and report."@en ,
                 "Outcome: Licensing compliant (CC0 deck, Wikidata the only content source, all other sources verification only). Four documentation precision suggestions, all applied after checking: Q261543 and Q14192234 sv labels re-fetched (\"Österrikes förbundsländer\", \"fastlandsterritorium i Australien\"), and the NE terms URL re-fetched (it ends at https://www.ne.se/info/upphovsratt/)."@en .

<#review-4>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-04T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Final full-deck review (facts and language)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: All 46 cards (capitals as of 2026-10-04, Swedish forms, language tags, notes), title, description, keywords, study direction, and the fixes of rounds 1–3."@en ,
                 "Outcome: All 46 capitals correct as of 2026-10-04, Swedish names established, tags and notes consistent, description accurate, and the fixes of rounds 1–3 confirmed present. One optional suggestion (a note on Salzburg's identical front and back), applied."@en .

<#review-5>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-10T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Version 2: title, description and keywords in Korean, German, Spanish and French (AI)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: the deck’s title, description and keywords, translated by an AI agent from the English (the Swedish settling what was ambiguous) into Korean, German, Spanish and French, in the words the app itself uses, and checked by a second AI agent that translated every text back into English and fixed what had drifted; the release compared by a script with version 1, which found the new title, description and keywords and the release’s own metadata the only changes, and checked by the library checker; not a human review."@en ,
                 "Outcome: the title, description and keywords are in Korean, German, Spanish and French as well; no card changed."@en .

